-- title:
--   Theorem 6.2 — exact contraction of $\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{LO}}$ and $\|\cdot\|_{W_1}$ under qubit tensor channels: coefficient $\max_i\|\Theta_i\|$
-- statement:
--   Let $E=\bigotimes_{i=1}^nE_i$, $n\ge1$, be a tensor product of qubit channels with Bloch matrices $\Theta_i$, and let $\|\Theta_i\|$ be the largest singular value of $\Theta_i$. For a Hermitian $H$, let $\kappa_i(H)$ and $\lambda_i(H)$ be the largest change of $\operatorname{Tr}[H\,\cdot\,]$ under one move at register $i$: over pairs $\rho\sim_i\sigma$ of neighboring states, respectively over pairs with $\operatorname{Tr}_i\rho=\operatorname{Tr}_i\sigma$. Let $\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{LO}}$ and $\|\cdot\|_{W_1}$ be the transport norms generated by these two kinds of moves.
--
--   1. For every Hermitian $H$ and every $i\in[n]$,
--   $$\kappa_i(E^\dagger H)\le\|\Theta_i\|\,\kappa_i(H),\qquad \lambda_i(E^\dagger H)\le\|\Theta_i\|\,\lambda_i(H).\tag{36}$$
--   2. The contraction coefficients of both norms are exactly the worst one-qubit factor:
--   $$\sup_{X\ne0}\frac{\|E(X)\|_{\mathrm{LO}}}{\|X\|_{\mathrm{LO}}}=\sup_{X\ne0}\frac{\|E(X)\|_{W_1}}{\|X\|_{W_1}}=\max_{i\in[n]}\|\Theta_i\|,$$
--   the suprema over nonzero traceless Hermitian $X$ on $(\mathbb C^2)^{\otimes n}$.
--
--   The coefficient sees only the linear part of each channel, so nonunital noise costs nothing extra. For example, the amplitude-damping channel with damping probability $\eta$ has coefficient $\sqrt{1-\eta}$ in both norms for every $n$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - encoding: i ∈ [n], max_{i∈[n]} → hypothesis 0 < n; reason: the maximum over [n] needs n ≥ 1; it excludes only the undefined case n = 0
--   - encoding: sup_{X≠0} ∥E(X)∥/∥X∥ = max_i ∥Θ_i∥ → IsLUB of the set of ratios over nonzero traceless Hermitian X, with value ⨆ i, specNorm (blochMatrix (E i)); reason: IsLUB says the supremum exists and equals the value, without the real sSup default; the norms are defined on traceless Hermitian operators
--   - encoding: ∥X∥_LO, ∥X∥_W1: the smallest c ≥ 0 with X ∈ c · conv(C_LO), resp. conv(C_EM) → sInf {c | 0 ≤ c ∧ X ∈ c • convexHull ℝ C}; reason: the infimum is the smallest such c (it is attained); the set is nonempty for traceless Hermitian X when n ≥ 1
--   - encoding: κ_i(H), λ_i(H) as suprema of Tr[H(ρ − σ)] → sSup of the real parts of the traces; reason: the sets are nonempty (ρ = σ) and bounded (density operators), and the traces are real for Hermitian H
--   - encoding: Bloch matrices Θ_i, ∥Θ_i∥ largest singular value; E†H → blochMatrix (E i), specNorm; pullback (tensorChannel E) H; reason: the definitions of the supplement model and the base Hilbert–Schmidt adjoint
-- source:
--   Ji Guan, Yecheng Qin, Parallel Composition of Quantum Differential Privacy: The Role of Measurement Restrictions, STOC 2027 submission #1640 (October 2026), source.pdf SHA-256 da23c8347251683a16df4c61de3fa1604211cdbf34d757a7a45feb0efd54c694, Theorem 6.2 (printed p. 32 / PDF p. 33), proof printed pp. 32–33 / PDF pp. 33–34; definitions §6.1 (printed p. 31 / PDF p. 32)

import Definitions.Def_GuanQinQDP_Restricted_Supplement_Model
open QAlgorithms GuanQinQDP.Restricted WildeQIT.EntBreaking
open scoped Matrix ComplexOrder

namespace GuanQinQDP.Restricted.Supplement

/-- Theorem 6.2 (Exact contraction of the transport norms), Guan–Qin, STOC 2027 submission
#1640, printed p. 32 / PDF p. 33.

Let `E = ⨂_{i=1}^n E_i` (`n ≥ 1`) be a tensor product of qubit channels with Bloch matrices
`Θ_i`.

1. (36) For every Hermitian `H` and every `i`, `κ_i(E†H) ≤ ∥Θ_i∥ κ_i(H)` and
   `λ_i(E†H) ≤ ∥Θ_i∥ λ_i(H)`.
2. `sup_{X ≠ 0} ∥E(X)∥_LO / ∥X∥_LO = max_i ∥Θ_i∥`, the supremum over nonzero traceless
   Hermitian `X`.
3. `sup_{X ≠ 0} ∥E(X)∥_W1 / ∥X∥_W1 = max_i ∥Θ_i∥`, likewise. -/
theorem transport_contraction {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n)
    (E : Fin n → (Matrix Qubit Qubit ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix Qubit Qubit ℂ))
    (hE : ∀ i, IsQuantumChannel (E i)) :
    (∀ H : Matrix (Fin n → Qubit) (Fin n → Qubit) ℂ, H.IsHermitian → ∀ i : Fin n,
      kappa i (pullback (tensorChannel E) H) ≤ specNorm (blochMatrix ⇑(E i)) * kappa i H ∧
      lambdaEM i (pullback (tensorChannel E) H) ≤ specNorm (blochMatrix ⇑(E i)) * lambdaEM i H) ∧
    IsLUB {x : ℝ | ∃ X : Matrix (Fin n → Qubit) (Fin n → Qubit) ℂ,
        X.IsHermitian ∧ X.trace = 0 ∧ X ≠ 0 ∧ x = normLO (tensorChannel E X) / normLO X}
      (⨆ i : Fin n, specNorm (blochMatrix ⇑(E i))) ∧
    IsLUB {x : ℝ | ∃ X : Matrix (Fin n → Qubit) (Fin n → Qubit) ℂ,
        X.IsHermitian ∧ X.trace = 0 ∧ X ≠ 0 ∧ x = normW1 (tensorChannel E X) / normW1 X}
      (⨆ i : Fin n, specNorm (blochMatrix ⇑(E i))) := by sorry

end GuanQinQDP.Restricted.Supplement
